From: Andrew Hunt <achunt@bellsouth.net>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 09:45:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Adapt service, HAL-wait and make-clean for LuneOS

Three adaptations on top of upstream c3e1b15:

1. Makefile - "rm bluebinder" -> "rm -f bluebinder". bitbake's do_configure
   runs "make clean" before anything has been built, and the bare rm fails
   with "cannot remove 'bluebinder': No such file or directory". (Carried
   over from the old 0001-Use-CC-as-compiler.patch; the $(CC) half of that
   patch is now obsolete because upstream's Makefile uses $(CC) itself.)

2. bluebinder.service - point at LuneOS paths and ordering:
   - After=android-system.service (LuneOS) rather than droid-hal-init.service
     (Sailfish), which does not exist here.
   - Helper scripts live in ${sbindir}, not /usr/bin/droid.
   - Drop ExecStartPost: bluebinder_post.sh derives the adapter address from
     ro.bt.bdaddr_path / ro.vendor.bt.bdaddr_path / persist.vendor.service.
     bdroid.bdaddr, and bluejay (Pixel 6a) sets NONE of them - the AIDL HAL
     provisions the address itself - so it would always exit 1 and fail the
     unit. Re-add it for any port that does expose those properties.
   - Drop the sandboxing block, matching the previous LuneOS adaptation, so
     first bring-up is not fighting DevicePolicy=strict at the same time.
     Worth restoring (it needs /dev/binder, /dev/hwbinder, /dev/vhci,
     /dev/rfkill) once this is known-good.
   - WantedBy=multi-user.target; LuneOS has no graphical.target.

3. bluebinder_wait.sh - upstream only matches Android service names containing
   "bluetooth". On Broadcom/Pixel that name is "bcmbtlinux", so the loop never
   terminated and the unit hung in ExecStartPre forever. Match the common
   spellings instead, still excluding the separate bluetooth.audio HAL.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [distro/device-specific paths]
---
diff --git a/Makefile b/Makefile
index 988a2d4..34f8018 100644
--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -18,5 +18,5 @@ install:
 	cp bluebinder $(DESTDIR)/usr/sbin
 
 clean:
-	rm bluebinder
+	rm -f bluebinder
 
diff --git a/bluebinder.service b/bluebinder.service
index 1ee68f7..a73a72d 100644
--- a/bluebinder.service
+++ b/bluebinder.service
@@ -1,29 +1,15 @@
 [Unit]
 Description=Simple proxy for using android binder based bluetooth through vhci.
-After=droid-hal-init.service
+After=android-system.service
 Before=bluetooth.service
 
 [Service]
 Type=notify
 EnvironmentFile=-/var/lib/environment/bluebinder/*.conf
-ExecStartPre=/usr/bin/droid/bluebinder_wait.sh
+ExecStartPre=/usr/sbin/bluebinder_wait.sh
 ExecStart=/usr/sbin/bluebinder
-ExecStartPost=/usr/bin/droid/bluebinder_post.sh
 Restart=always
 TimeoutStartSec=60
-# Sandboxing
-CapabilityBoundingSet=CAP_DAC_READ_SEARCH
-DeviceAllow=/dev/binder rw
-DeviceAllow=/dev/hwbinder rw
-DeviceAllow=/dev/vhci rw
-DeviceAllow=/dev/rfkill r
-DevicePolicy=strict
-NoNewPrivileges=yes
-RestrictAddressFamilies=AF_BLUETOOTH
-PrivateTmp=yes
-ProtectHome=yes
-ProtectSystem=full
 
 [Install]
-WantedBy=graphical.target
-
+WantedBy=multi-user.target
diff --git a/bluebinder_wait.sh b/bluebinder_wait.sh
index d7a059d..dbc0fff 100755
--- a/bluebinder_wait.sh
+++ b/bluebinder_wait.sh
@@ -1,13 +1,26 @@
 #!/bin/sh
 
+# Wait for the Android-side Bluetooth HAL service to report running.
+#
+# The service name is device-specific. Upstream only matched names containing
+# "bluetooth", which is wrong on Broadcom/Pixel devices: bluejay (Pixel 6a)
+# names it "bcmbtlinux", so the original loop here span forever and the unit
+# never started. Match the common spellings instead.
+#
+# The separate bluetooth.audio HAL is excluded deliberately - it can be running
+# while the HCI HAL is not, which would let us start too early.
+#
+# init.svc_debug_pid.* lines also match the name pattern, but their value is a
+# pid rather than [running], so the [running] filter drops them.
+
 while true
 do
-    /usr/bin/getprop | grep -q init.svc.*.bluetooth.audio
-    if [ $? -eq 0 ] ; then
-        bt_status=$(/usr/bin/getprop |grep "init.svc.*bluetooth" |grep -v audio |grep -o "\[running\]")
-    else
-        bt_status=$(/usr/bin/getprop |grep "init.svc.*bluetooth" |grep -o "\[running\]")
-    fi
+    bt_status=$(/usr/bin/getprop \
+        | grep -E "init\.svc\.[^]]*(bluetooth|btlinux|bt-hal|bt_hal)" \
+        | grep -v audio \
+        | grep -o "\[running\]" \
+        | head -n 1)
+
     if [ "$bt_status" = "[running]" ] ; then
         echo "Bluetooth service running"
         exit 0
